; companion to forall-elim-cannot-prove-arbitrary-equality.kurt: confirms the fix for that bug
; (blocking forall-elim's own eigenvariable from being resolved to a specific value during its
; premise search) didn't overcorrect into breaking genuine forall-elim usage. A real
; universally-quantified fact must still instantiate at a specific value.
load logic
bool P
arity P 1
const P, c

use ∀ $x P $x
P c
;;; Proof checked.
